## Retry policy[^policy]

Retries are capped at five[^retries], as the SRE review asked[^SRE]. The cap is the same for every
queue[^retries], and the review is linked again here[^sre].

Not footnotes: `[^retries]` in code, a [^retries](https://example.com/retries) link and a
[^retries]{color=red} span.

<!-- smd-disable-next-line footnote/undefined -->
A label nobody defined stays text: [^missing].

| Queue  | Retries        |
| ------ | -------------- |
| emails | 5[^retries]    |
| sms    | 3[^sms-limits] |

:::warning Rate limits
The provider throttles bursts[^burst].

[^burst]: Defined inside the callout; rendered with the others at the end.
:::

::::tabs
:::tab Staging
Staging retries faster[^staging].
:::
:::tab Production
Production backs off exponentially.
:::
::::

## Notes

[^policy]: Agreed in the 2026-09 incident review.
[^retries]: Five covers 99.9% of transient failures in last quarter's logs.
[^sre]: SRE review, 2026-09-12.
    Lines indented by 4 spaces continue the footnote.

    A second paragraph, with a list:

    - backoff doubles each time
    - jitter is ±20%
[^sms-limits]: The SMS provider allows three attempts per message.
[^staging]: Staging uses a 100 ms base delay instead of 1 s.

<!-- smd-disable-next-line footnote/unused -->
[^draft]: Not referenced anywhere, so it is not shown.
